{
    "title": "WICShopper",
    "description": "PLEASE READ! WICShopper CURRENTLY SUPPORTS THE WIC PROGRAMS IN THE FOLLOWING STATES:\r\n\r\nAlaska\r\nConnecticut \r\nColorado\r\nFlorida\r\nHawaii\r\nIdaho\r\nIowa\r\nITC Arizona\r\nKansas\r\nKentucky\r\nLouisiana\r\nMaine \r\nMassachusetts\r\nMississippi\r\nMissouri \r\nMontana\r\nNebraska\r\nNevada\r\nNevada ITC\r\nNew Hampshire \r\nNew Jersey\r\nOhio\r\nOregon\r\nPassamaquoddy Tribe Pleasant Point \r\nPennsylvania\r\nRhode Island \r\nTennessee \r\nUtah \r\nVermont (Verification only)\r\nWashington\r\nWest Virginia\r\nWyoming\r\n\r\n\r\nWICShopper WILL NOT WORK IN OTHER STATES.  We are adding new states all the time, so please check back soon if you participate in another WIC program!\r\n\r\nGrocery shopping for foods allowed by your WIC* program can be confusing.  Much of the problem is from not knowing exactly what products you can purchase with your WIC benefits. WICShopper is here to help you shop with confidence. Using WICShopper, you can check the WIC eligibility of products while you shop! In all of our supported WIC programs, you can use your phone to scan products to check their WIC eligibility. \r\n\r\nIn most supported states, you may register your eWIC card, then automatically download your CURRENT benefits every time you shop! WICShopper doesn\u2019t just tell you if the product is WIC eligible\u2026 it tells you if you have enough WIC benefits left to purchase the product! \r\n\r\nIn states that use \"smart cards\" such as Texas, New Mexico and Wyoming it is not possible to load your prescription because it is stored on your card.  In these states, you can use the app to capture and store an image of your benefits to use the next time you shop.\r\n\r\nWe are adding new states as quickly as possible, so if your state isn't listed please check back soon! To learn more about WICShopper, please visit our website @ www.ebtshopper.com. \r\n\r\n* Special Supplemental Nutrition Program for Women, Infants, and Children",
    "descriptionHTML": "PLEASE READ! WICShopper CURRENTLY SUPPORTS THE WIC PROGRAMS IN THE FOLLOWING STATES:<br><br>Alaska<br>Connecticut <br>Colorado<br>Florida<br>Hawaii<br>Idaho<br>Iowa<br>ITC Arizona<br>Kansas<br>Kentucky<br>Louisiana<br>Maine <br>Massachusetts<br>Mississippi<br>Missouri <br>Montana<br>Nebraska<br>Nevada<br>Nevada ITC<br>New Hampshire <br>New Jersey<br>Ohio<br>Oregon<br>Passamaquoddy Tribe Pleasant Point <br>Pennsylvania<br>Rhode Island <br>Tennessee <br>Utah <br>Vermont (Verification only)<br>Washington<br>West Virginia<br>Wyoming<br><br><br>WICShopper WILL NOT WORK IN OTHER STATES.  We are adding new states all the time, so please check back soon if you participate in another WIC program!<br><br>Grocery shopping for foods allowed by your WIC* program can be confusing.  Much of the problem is from not knowing exactly what products you can purchase with your WIC benefits. WICShopper is here to help you shop with confidence. Using WICShopper, you can check the WIC eligibility of products while you shop! In all of our supported WIC programs, you can use your phone to scan products to check their WIC eligibility. <br><br>In most supported states, you may register your eWIC card, then automatically download your CURRENT benefits every time you shop! WICShopper doesn\u2019t just tell you if the product is WIC eligible\u2026 it tells you if you have enough WIC benefits left to purchase the product! <br><br>In states that use &quot;smart cards&quot; such as Texas, New Mexico and Wyoming it is not possible to load your prescription because it is stored on your card.  In these states, you can use the app to capture and store an image of your benefits to use the next time you shop.<br><br>We are adding new states as quickly as possible, so if your state isn&#39;t listed please check back soon! To learn more about WICShopper, please visit our website @ www.ebtshopper.com. <br><br>* Special Supplemental Nutrition Program for Women, Infants, and Children",
